---
interface Props {
  /** A fonts.googleapis.com css2 URL. */
  href: string;
}

const { href } = Astro.props;
---

{/*
  Google's font stylesheet, fetched without blocking the first paint.

  A plain <link rel="stylesheet"> to a third-party origin holds up rendering until it
  resolves, which made first paint a direct function of Google's response time: an
  injected 2.5s delay on this request moved FCP from 612ms to 3032ms, while our own
  server's TTFB never moved off ~120ms. That is how /resume scored 76 on a run where
  every metric we control was perfect.

  `rel="preload" as="style"` fetches at high priority without blocking, then onload
  promotes it to a real stylesheet. Clearing onload first stops the handler re-firing
  when the rel change triggers a second load event in some browsers.

  The font arrives after first paint either way, so text paints in the fallback and
  swaps -- which is why the fallback stacks are metric-matched (see resume.astro).
*/}
<link
  rel="preload"
  as="style"
  href={href}
  onload="this.onload=null;this.rel='stylesheet'"
/>
<noscript><link rel="stylesheet" href={href} /></noscript>
